{
  "id": "dsa-007",
  "title": "Functions in programming - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A function is a block of code that performs a specific task and can be reused whenever needed.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Avoids writing the same code again and again.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Makes programs simple and easy to understand by breaking into smaller parts.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Accepts input (parameters) and gives output.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Finding and fixing errors become easier.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"function1\" data-resized=\"true\" height=\"400\" src=\"./images/dsa-007-img-1.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260318170520103377/function1.webp 800w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260318170520103377/function1-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260318170520103377/function1-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260318170520103377/function1-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260318170520103377/function1-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260318170520103377/function1-768.webp 768w\" width=\"800\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"builtin-functions\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Built-in functions</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>These are predefined functions provided by programming languages or libraries to perform common tasks such as mathematical calculations, input/output, or string operations.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>For example, the sqrt() function from the C++ &lt;cmath&gt; library calculates the square root of a number.</span></li></ul><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C++</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"cpp\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-cpp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">std</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// built-in function</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">25.0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">  </span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">cout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Square Root: \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">endl</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"c\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-c\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// built-in function</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">25.0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Square Root: %.2lf</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">Java</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"java\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-java\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">java.lang.Math</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">GFG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// built-in function</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">25.0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Square Root: \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">Python</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"python3\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-python3\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"nn\">math</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># built-in function</span>\n<span class=\"n\">result</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">math</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">25.0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Square Root:\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C#</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"csharp\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-csharp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">System</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">GFG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// built-in function</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">25.0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WriteLine</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Square Root: \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">JavaScript</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"c1\">// built-in function</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">25.0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Square Root: \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">result</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><div class=\"code-output\"><br><strong>Output</strong><pre>Square Root: 5\n</pre></div><h3 id=\"userdefined\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>User-defined functions</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>These functions are functions written by programmers to perform specific tasks required in a program. </span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>They help organize code and allow reuse of logic whenever needed.</span></li></ul><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C++</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"cpp\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-cpp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">std</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">cout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello, World!\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">endl</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">// calling user-defined function</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"c\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-c\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello, World!</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// calling user-defined function</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">Java</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"java\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-java\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">GFG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello, World!\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// calling user-defined function</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">Python</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"python3\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-python3\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"k\">def</span> <span class=\"nf\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">():</span>\n    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Hello, World!\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"vm\">__name__</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"__main__\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"c1\"># Calling user-defined function.</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C#</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"csharp\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-csharp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">System</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">GFG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WriteLine</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello, World!\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// calling user-defined function</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">JavaScript</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'Hello, World!'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">// calling user-defined function</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><div class=\"code-output\"><br><strong>Output</strong><pre>Hello, World!\n</pre></div><h3 id=\"function-visualizer\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Function Visualizer</span></h3><style>\nh2, h3, p {\nmargin-bottom: 6px !important;\n}\n\n/* Iframe */\n#iframe-container1 {\nwidth: 100%;\nmax-width: 600px;\nborder: none;\ndisplay: block;\noverflow: hidden;\nheight: 580px; /* default */\n}\n\n/* Small screens (mobile) */\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n#iframe-container1 {\nheight: 680px;\n}\n}\n\n/* Medium screens (tablet) */\n@media (min-width: 481px) and (max-width: 900px) {\n#iframe-container1 {\nheight: 420px;\n}\n}\n\n/* Large screens */\n@media (min-width: 901px) and (max-width: 1400px) {\n#iframe-container1 {\nheight: 400px;\n}\n}\n\n/* Extra large screens */\n@media (min-width: 1401px) {\n#iframe-container1 {\nheight: 420px;\n}\n}\n</style><h4 id=\"where-are-functions-used-in-dsa\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Where are Functions Used in DSA?</span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>In DSA, functions are used to implement algorithms and solve problems in a structured and reusable way.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Implement algorithms like searching and sorting.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Handle recursion (like factorial, tree traversal).</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Break problems into smaller subproblems.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Operate on data structures like arrays, linked lists, trees, and graphs.</span></li><li value=\"5\"><span>Make code clean and easy to understand.</span></li></ul></div>",
  "textContent": "A function is a block of code that performs a specific task and can be reused whenever needed.Avoids writing the same code again and again.Makes programs simple and easy to understand by breaking into smaller parts.Accepts input (parameters) and gives output.Finding and fixing errors become easier. Built-in functionsThese are predefined functions provided by programming languages or libraries to perform common tasks such as mathematical calculations, input/output, or string operations.For example, the sqrt() function from the C++ <cmath> library calculates the square root of a number.\n            C++\n\n    #include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    \n    // built-in function\n    double result = sqrt(25.0);  \n    cout << \"Square Root: \" << result << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n\n\n            C\n\n    #include <math.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main()\n{\n    // built-in function\n    double result = sqrt(25.0);\n    printf(\"Square Root: %.2lf\\n\", result);\n    return 0;\n}\n\n\n            Java\n\n    import java.lang.Math;\n\npublic class GFG {\n    public static void main(String[] args)\n    {\n        // built-in function\n        double result = Math.sqrt(25.0);\n        System.out.println(\"Square Root: \" + result);\n    }\n}\n\n\n            Python\n\n    import math\n\n# built-in function\nresult = math.sqrt(25.0)\nprint(\"Square Root:\", result)\n\n\n            C#\n\n    using System;\n\nclass GFG {\n    static void Main()\n    {\n        // built-in function\n        double result = Math.Sqrt(25.0);\n        Console.WriteLine(\"Square Root: \" + result);\n    }\n}\n\n\n            JavaScript\n\n    // built-in function\nlet result = Math.sqrt(25.0);\nconsole.log(\"Square Root: \" + result);\n\nOutputSquare Root: 5\nUser-defined functionsThese functions are functions written by programmers to perform specific tasks required in a program. They help organize code and allow reuse of logic whenever needed.\n            C++\n\n    #include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nvoid greet() {\n    cout << \"Hello, World!\" << endl;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    greet();  // calling user-defined function\n    return 0;\n}\n\n\n            C\n\n    #include <stdio.h>\n\nvoid greet()\n{\n    printf(\"Hello, World!\\n\");\n}\n\nint main()\n{\n    greet(); // calling user-defined function\n    return 0;\n}\n\n\n            Java\n\n    public class GFG {\n    public static void greet()\n    {\n        System.out.println(\"Hello, World!\");\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args)\n    {\n        greet(); // calling user-defined function\n    }\n}\n\n\n            Python\n\n    def greet():\n    print(\"Hello, World!\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Calling user-defined function.\n    greet()\n\n\n            C#\n\n    using System;\n\nclass GFG {\n    static void greet()\n    {\n        Console.WriteLine(\"Hello, World!\");\n    }\n\n    static void Main()\n    {\n        greet(); // calling user-defined function\n    }\n}\n\n\n            JavaScript\n\n    function greet() {\n    console.log('Hello, World!');\n}\n\n// calling user-defined function\ngreet();\n\nOutputHello, World!\nFunction Visualizer\nh2, h3, p {\nmargin-bottom: 6px !important;\n}\n\n/* Iframe */\n#iframe-container1 {\nwidth: 100%;\nmax-width: 600px;\nborder: none;\ndisplay: block;\noverflow: hidden;\nheight: 580px; /* default */\n}\n\n/* Small screens (mobile) */\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n#iframe-container1 {\nheight: 680px;\n}\n}\n\n/* Medium screens (tablet) */\n@media (min-width: 481px) and (max-width: 900px) {\n#iframe-container1 {\nheight: 420px;\n}\n}\n\n/* Large screens */\n@media (min-width: 901px) and (max-width: 1400px) {\n#iframe-container1 {\nheight: 400px;\n}\n}\n\n/* Extra large screens */\n@media (min-width: 1401px) {\n#iframe-container1 {\nheight: 420px;\n}\n}\nWhere are Functions Used in DSA?In DSA, functions are used to implement algorithms and solve problems in a structured and reusable way.Implement algorithms like searching and sorting.Handle recursion (like factorial, tree traversal).Break problems into smaller subproblems.Operate on data structures like arrays, linked lists, trees, and graphs.Make code clean and easy to understand.",
